19	@eslint/js	v10.x requires eslint v10; typescript-eslint/import/react plugins lack v10 peer dep support
22	@astrojs/react	6.x is a major on the Astro integration stack while astro itself is deliberately held on the 5 line (see the astro entry below); move it with that migration, not standalone. Only the major is blocked — in-range 5.0.x patches still upgrade normally.
23	@astrojs/mdx	v5.x requires astro@^6.0.0; we are on astro 5.x and astro v6 migration is not scheduled
24	astro	www is built on the astro 5 line; v6/v7 are breaking majors covering the whole site build — same unscheduled-migration hold as @astrojs/mdx, take them together as a dedicated project
27	glob	root overrides force glob ^11 tree-wide and npm EOVERRIDE requires the declared devDep range to equal the override, so the v13 major cannot be taken until the override family is re-evaluated
30	@types/node	v25+ targets Node 25 APIs; our engines field and CI runners are on Node 22
33	eslint-plugin-unicorn	v66 is a major release that adds and renames lint rules which would surface new violations across the whole monorepo; adoption deferred to a dedicated lint-tooling PR that audits and fixes the rule-set changes
36	playwright	a playwright version bump changes the bundled browser revisions, so it is never a drop-in dependency bump — the pinned browsers must be re-downloaded (npx playwright install) and the E2E/bridge suites re-validated against the new revisions in the same change; take any future bump together with that test-infra revalidation
37	@playwright/test	same hold as playwright above, and not a separate judgement call — @playwright/test@X depends on playwright@X pinned EXACTLY (verified: @playwright/test@1.62.0 -> "playwright": "1.62.0"), so upgrading it upgrades the browser revisions the entry above defers. Listing only `playwright` left the gate demanding the bump through its sibling; move both with the E2E/bridge revalidation.
39	eslint	v10 requires typescript-eslint/import/react plugin majors that have no eslint v10 peer support yet; take together with @eslint/js in a dedicated lint-tooling PR
